# Sample Memory Access Trace
# Format: <type> <address_hex> <size>
# l = load (read), s = store (write)
#
# Scenario 1: Spatial locality (sequential access within the same 16-byte block 0x1000-0x100F)
l 0x1000 4
s 0x1004 4
l 0x1008 4
s 0x100C 4

# Scenario 2: Temporal locality (re-accessing previously cached block)
l 0x1000 4
s 0x1004 4

# Scenario 3: Accessing new memory block (Miss)
l 0x2000 4
l 0x2004 4

# Scenario 4: Set index conflict demonstration
# With 256 sets and 16-byte blocks:
# offset_bits = 4, index_bits = 8.
# address >> 4 & 0xFF gives set index.
# Addresses 0x1000 (set 0) and 0x2000 (set 0) share the same set!
l 0x3000 4
l 0x4000 4
l 0x5000 4
